{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CQuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CQuantumUniverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.reeb_preserves_contact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.reeb_preserves_contact","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The Reeb field preserves the contact form: θ(ξ(p)) = θ(p) for all p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.reebField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.reebField","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The Reeb vector field `ξ`, characterised by `ι_ξ dθ = 0` and `θ(ξ) = 1`.\nModelled as a continuous self-map `M → M` (the Reeb flow at time 1).\nFull type: a section of `TM`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.contact_nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.contact_nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The contact form is non-degenerate: there exists a point where θ ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.contactForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.contactForm","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The contact form `θ` as a real-valued function on `M`.\nFull type: a section of `T*M` (1-form), here modelled as a map `M → ℝ`.\nThe contact condition `θ ∧ (dθ)^n ≠ 0` is a non-degeneracy axiom\nthat requires differential forms; we record θ as a function\nand state the non-degeneracy separately.\n\nWas `M → R_q`, with a note that \"the ground ring `R_q` carries no\ncanonical topology\". True, and the reason not to put a contact form\nthere: a contact form is a real 1-form, and `ι_ξ dθ = 0`, `θ(ξ) = 1` and\n`θ ∧ (dθ)^n ≠ 0` all need the real structure. §7c reserves `ℝ` for\narchimedean constructs and this is one; the library copy always had `ℝ`\n(bean `qou-u87j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.rs_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.rs_sum","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.s","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.r","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Levi form signature `(r, s)` with `r + s = n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.n_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.n_pos","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L64-L64","doc":"`n ≥ 1`, as the docstring above already claimed.\n\nRestored (bean `qou-u87j`). This field had been commented out as\n\"`-- n_pos : 0 < n  -- (archimedean; not meaningful over R_q)`\", and that\njustification is simply wrong: `n` is a **natural number**, the CR\ndimension, and `0 < n` says nothing about `R_q` either way. A §7c sweep\nremoved an anti-vacuity condition it had misread. Without it a\n\"CR manifold\" of dimension `0` satisfies the structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.n","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L55-L55","doc":"CR dimension `n ≥ 1`; real dimension of `M` is `2n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.topM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.topM","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.M","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The underlying smooth manifold carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L42-L89","doc":"**CR manifold data** for the ℂ realisation.\n\nCanonical 4-tuple `(C, θ, G, S)`: `C = Rep(SU_q(2))` is the monoidal\ncategory; `θ` is the contact form (pseudo-Hermitian structure) on a\nCR manifold `M` (implicit as domain of `θ`); `G = SU(2)`;\n`S = P ×_G CP¹` is the state bundle (principal bundle `P` implicit).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:c-quantum-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:c-quantum-universe","label":"ex:c-quantum-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}